 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Bounded-below truncation criterion",
 "statement": "Let $K\\in D^+_{\\mathcal P\\text{-tor}}(T_{\\Et})$. For fixed $n$, only\n$H^q(K)$ with $q\\leq n$ can contribute to $H^n(Rg_*K)$. Hence\n\n$$\nH^n(Rg_*\\tau_{\\leq n}K)\\xrightarrow{\\ \\sim\\ }H^n(Rg_*K),\n$$\n\nand the analogous statement holds after pullback and for $h_*$.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-smooth-base-change/sk-rem-rest/sbc-lem-bounded-below-truncation-criterion.md",
  "place": "node sbc-lem-bounded-below-truncation-criterion, order 1439"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "sbc-def-derived-categories-with-allowable-torsion"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "The hypercohomology spectral sequence of\n[def-weil-pbc-hypercohomology-filtrations] has\n$E_2^{p,q}=R^pg_*H^q(K)$; for $p+q=n$ only $q\\leq n$ contributes since\n$g_*$ is $t$-left exact, so\n$H^n(Rg_*\\tau_{\\leq n}K)\\cong H^n(Rg_*K)$; pullback and $h$ are handled\nidentically.",
   "uses": [
    "def-weil-pbc-hypercohomology-filtrations"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
